1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:00,972
Lesson two.

2
00:00:00,972 --> 00:00:04,411
Many beginners try everything and master nothing.

3
00:00:04,411 --> 00:00:08,200
Today you will choose one skill using a simple method.

4
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:10,851
Ask yourself three questions.

5
00:00:10,851 --> 00:00:12,869
What am I already good at?

6
00:00:12,869 --> 00:00:14,654
What do people pay for?

7
00:00:14,654 --> 00:00:19,000
And what can I practise every day without getting bored?

8
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:21,772
Make a list of your strengths.

9
00:00:21,772 --> 00:00:29,363
The languages you speak, the tools you already use, and the things friends ask you to help with.

10
00:00:29,363 --> 00:00:33,000
Your first skill is often hidden in that list.

11
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:35,005
Then check the demand.

12
00:00:35,005 --> 00:00:42,736
Search for the skill on job and freelance platforms, count the real offers, and read what clients ask for.

13
00:00:42,736 --> 00:00:45,800
If nobody is asking, choose another skill.

14
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:47,625
Pick a small niche.

15
00:00:47,625 --> 00:00:50,850
Not just design, but logos for small shops.

16
00:00:50,850 --> 00:00:54,075
Not just writing, but product descriptions.

17
00:00:54,075 --> 00:00:58,200
A small niche is easier to explain, and easier to sell.

18
00:00:58,600 --> 00:00:59,985
Learn with a plan.

19
00:00:59,985 --> 00:01:06,446
Thirty minutes every day, one small project every week, and free official tutorials.

20
00:01:06,446 --> 00:01:10,600
Use AI as a tutor, but always check what it tells you.

21
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,336
One skill, one niche, one plan.

22
00:01:13,336 --> 00:01:14,994
Write them down today.

23
00:01:14,994 --> 00:01:21,400
Next lesson: how to build a simple profile and portfolio that make clients trust you.

